\[
\Phi(t,\theta_0)
= \left(r_0 + Ce^{-\Lambda t}\right)
\begin{pmatrix}
\cos(\omega t + \theta_0) \\
\sin(\omega t + \theta_0)
\end{pmatrix}.
\]



Compute the tangent vectors:


\[
\Phi_t = \frac{\partial \Phi}{\partial t},
\qquad
\Phi_{\theta_0} = \frac{\partial \Phi}{\partial \theta_0}.
\]



The induced metric is


\[
g =
\begin{pmatrix}
\langle \Phi_t, \Phi_t \rangle & \langle \Phi_t, \Phi_{\theta_0} \rangle \\
\langle \Phi_{\theta_0}, \Phi_t \rangle & \langle \Phi_{\theta_0}, \Phi_{\theta_0} \rangle
\end{pmatrix}.
\]



Explicitly:


\[
\langle \Phi_{\theta_0}, \Phi_{\theta_0} \rangle
= \left(r_0 + Ce^{-\Lambda t}\right)^2.
\]





\[
\langle \Phi_t, \Phi_t \rangle
= (\Lambda C e^{-\Lambda t})^2
+ \left(r_0 + Ce^{-\Lambda t}\right)^2 \omega^2.
\]





\[
\langle \Phi_t, \Phi_{\theta_0} \rangle
= \left(r_0 + Ce^{-\Lambda t}\right)^2 \omega.
\]



Thus the metric tensor is


\[
g(t,\theta_0)
=
\begin{pmatrix}
(\Lambda C e^{-\Lambda t})^2 + (r_0 + Ce^{-\Lambda t})^2\omega^2
&
(r_0 + Ce^{-\Lambda t})^2\omega
\

\[6pt]
(r_0 + Ce^{-\Lambda t})^2\omega
&
(r_0 + Ce^{-\Lambda t})^2
\end{pmatrix}.
\]



