\subsection{Stable Manifold as a Fiber}

Define the projection


\[
\pi : W^s(\mathcal{C}) \to \mathcal{C},
\qquad
\pi(x) = \lim_{t\to\infty} \Phi_t(x).
\]



This is a morphism in $\mathbf{Dyn}$.

Thus $W^s(\mathcal{C})$ is a fiber bundle over $\mathcal{C}$.

% ------------------------------------------------------------
\subsection{D8-Equivariance}

Let $D_8$ act on $\mathbb{R}^2$ by rotations and reflections.

Define the functor


\[
F : D_8 \to \mathbf{Dyn},
\qquad
F(g) = (g, Dg).
\]



The CGHDS is $D_8$-equivariant if


\[
Dg \circ X = X \circ g
\quad\forall g \in D_8.
\]



Since


\[
V(gx) = V(x),
\qquad
Rgx = gRx,
\]


we have


\[
Dg \circ X = X \circ g.
\]



Thus $\mathcal{G}$ is a $D_8$-equivariant object.

