For the CGHDS:


\[
\mathcal{F}_{\text{golden}}(\mathcal{G})
= \mathcal{C}.
\]



Thus the golden ring is the image of the CGHDS under the golden functor.

% ------------------------------------------------------------
\subsection{Golden Natural Transformation}

Define the natural transformation


\[
\eta : \mathrm{Id}_{\mathbf{Dyn}} \Rightarrow \mathcal{F}_{\text{golden}}
\]


by


\[
\eta_{(M,X)}(x)
= \lim_{t\to\infty} \Phi_t(x).
\]



For the CGHDS:


\[
\eta_{\mathcal{G}}(x)
= \lim_{t\to\infty} \Phi_t(x)
= \pi(x).
\]



Thus the stable manifold projection is the component of the golden natural transformation.

% ------------------------------------------------------------
\subsection{Universal Property of the Golden Cycle}

The golden cycle $\mathcal{C}$ satisfies the universal property:

For any $D_8$-equivariant dynamical system $(M,X)$ with a unique attracting cycle, there exists a unique morphism


\[
f : (M,X) \to (\mathcal{C},X|_{\mathcal{C}})
\]


such that


\[
\pi \circ f = \eta_{(M,X)}.
\]



Thus the golden cycle is a terminal object in the category of $D_8$-equivariant attractors.

